---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

// Keep in step with PrivacyPolicyView.swift in the app.
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy — Nutrient Logger"
  description="What Nutrient Logger keeps on your device, what leaves it, and why. No account, no ads, and your food log never leaves your phone."
>
  <article class="blog-post">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="post-header">
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <div class="post-meta">
          <span>Last updated November 9, 2026</span>
        </div>
      </header>
      <div class="post-content">
        <p>
          Nutrient Logger does not require an account or sign-in, and does not operate any server that
          your food log is sent to or stored on. Everything you log (foods, meals, weight, goals) is
          stored locally in the app's data store on your device.
        </p>
        <p>
          We do not sell your personal information, and we do not share what you eat, your weight, or
          any other data you enter with advertisers or other third parties.
        </p>

        <h2>What leaves your device, and why</h2>

        <h3>1. Anonymous product analytics (Firebase Analytics)</h3>
        <p>
          We log which screens and features are used (for example, that a food was logged, a barcode
          was scanned, or a premium feature was tapped) so we know what to improve. These events do not
          include the foods you log, your weight, or other personal details, and are not linked to your
          identity.
        </p>
        <p>Two things they do include:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>the words you type into food search, so we can improve search and add foods that are missing</li>
          <li>the diet and main focus you choose during setup, so we can see what helps people on each diet</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>2. Barcode lookups (Open Food Facts)</h3>
        <p>
          When you scan a packaged food's barcode, the barcode number is sent to the
          <a href="https://world.openfoodfacts.org/">Open Food Facts</a> public database to retrieve its
          nutrition information. No other information about you is sent with that request.
        </p>

        <h3>3. Apple Health, only if you turn it on</h3>
        <p>
          If you enable Health sync, your calorie, macro, and water data is written to Apple Health, and
          weight data can be imported from Health. This stays within Apple's Health system on your device
          and is governed by Apple's own Health privacy protections, not sent to us.
        </p>

        <h2>No ads</h2>
        <p>
          Nutrient Logger does not show ads. Free-tier users occasionally see a prompt suggesting Premium
          in a handful of screens throughout the app. It's not served by any ad network, and no
          information about you is sent anywhere to show it.
        </p>

        <h2>Your choices and contact</h2>
        <p>
          You can request details about what analytics data has been collected, or ask us to stop
          collecting it, by contacting us through the Support link at the bottom of the app's Profile
          tab.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you believe at any point that we are not following this privacy policy as stated, please
          contact us the same way.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
